><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251013103313+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251013103315+10'00'" name="f5b90b8c-7517-43b1-90fb-ef7486ca0c3e" page="14" coords="220.770721,652.315491,284.835114,652.315491,220.770721,642.535583,284.835114,642.535583,49.606308,639.843384,284.896729,639.843384,49.606308,630.063477,284.896729,630.063477,49.606308,627.427246,284.827301,627.427246,49.606308,617.647339,284.827301,617.647339,49.606308,614.955139,284.842163,614.955139,49.606308,605.175232,284.842163,605.175232,277.341614,604.406799,284.841522,604.406799,277.341614,597.887573,284.841522,597.887573,49.606308,602.483032,277.350464,602.483032,49.606308,592.703125,277.350464,592.703125,49.606308,590.066162,284.820190,590.066162,49.606308,580.286255,284.820190,580.286255,49.606308,577.594055,284.823486,577.594055,49.606308,567.814148,284.823486,567.814148,49.607315,565.121948,284.826538,565.121948,49.607315,555.342041,284.826538,555.342041,49.607315,552.649841,284.799103,552.649841,49.607315,542.869934,284.799103,542.869934,49.607315,540.233704,284.858276,540.233704,49.607315,530.453796,284.858276,530.453796,130.960602,529.628784,147.985428,529.628784,130.960602,523.109558,147.985428,523.109558,277.398285,529.628784,284.898193,529.628784,277.398285,523.109558,284.898193,523.109558,49.607315,527.761597,130.904892,527.761597,49.607315,517.981689,130.904892,517.981689,151.426697,527.760681,277.342651,527.760681,151.426697,517.980774,277.342651,517.980774,218.551117,517.213074,235.632156,517.213074,218.551117,510.693848,235.632156,510.693848,49.606308,515.288208,218.528519,515.288208,49.606308,505.508301,218.528519,505.508301,240.264496,515.288208,284.804779,515.288208,240.264496,505.508301,284.804779,505.508301,49.605576,502.872070,284.828003,502.872070,49.605576,493.092163,284.828003,493.092163,49.605576,490.399902,284.823608,490.399902,49.605576,480.619995,284.823608,480.619995,49.605576,477.927795,284.866577,477.927795,49.605576,468.147888,284.866577,468.147888,49.604584,465.455627,284.892822,465.455627,49.604584,455.675720,284.892822,455.675720,49.604584,453.039490,249.777130,453.039490,49.604584,443.259583,249.777130,443.259583" rect="49.298950,442.953949,285.202362,652.621094" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Across several&#xD;movement assessments, results suggest that youth athletes&#xD;can exhibit some improvements in non-sportspecific&#xD;competencies when supervised training is performed,&#xD;with all but one of the included studies</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>32&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>reporting some degree of positive changes in their&#xD;movement assessment. The findings of process-outcomes&#xD;in experimental studies complement previous&#xD;reviews, where the majority of exercise interventions&#xD;focused exclusively on outcomes of capacity or movement&#xD;product tests,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>19,57 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>recognised injury risk factors</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>58&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>or prospectively reported injury rates.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>18,59 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Therefore,&#xD;the current review calls for more studies to assess&#xD;movement competency in youth athletes with the inclusion&#xD;of movement process assessments alongside capacity&#xD;or product outcomes to complement the holistic&#xD;preparation strategies in athletic development.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
